      "hints": [
        "Set $S = \\frac{a}{1 - r} = \\frac{r^2 - 3r + 2}{1 - r}$.",
        "Factorise numerator $(r - 1)(r - 2) = -(1 - r)(r - 2)$ to show $S = 2 - r$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute the first term $a = r^2 - 3r + 2$ and common ratio $r$ into the sum to infinity formula:\n$$S = \\frac{a}{1 - r} = \\frac{r^2 - 3r + 2}{1 - r}$$",
        "Factorise the quadratic numerator:\n$$r^2 - 3r + 2 = (r - 1)(r - 2) = -(1 - r)(r - 2)$$",
        "Simplify by cancelling the common factor $(1 - r)$:\n$$S = \\frac{-(1 - r)(r - 2)}{1 - r} = -(r - 2) = 2 - r$$"
      ],
